chapter.v:
Take away 


from me, 


scorn and contempt, for I have kept your testimonies.

Let your 


steadfast love, 


come to me, O LORD, your salvation according to your promise;

When I 


think on, 


my ways, I turn my feet to your testimonies;

The insolent 


smear me, 


with lies, but with my whole heart I keep your precepts;

Redeem me 


from man’s, 


oppression, that I may keep your precepts.

I hope 


for your, 


salvation, O LORD, and I do your commandments.

I long 


for your, 


salvation, O LORD, and your law is my delight.
